{
  "tamil-nadus-water-infrastructure-runs": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Kaveri_Cauvery_River_Tamil_Nadu_India_May_2014.jpg/960px-Kaveri_Cauvery_River_Tamil_Nadu_India_May_2014.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"The Kaveri (Cauvery) river running through Tamil Nadu\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">The Kaveri is the river at the heart of the state's restoration and desilting spending this piece traces across three separate, non-matching funding streams. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kaveri_Cauvery_River_Tamil_Nadu_India_May_2014.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Kaveri Cauvery River Tamil Nadu India May 2014.jpg</a>, Bikash Das, CC BY 2.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "securitising-deficit-what-it-would": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Gold_bullion_bars.jpg/960px-Gold_bullion_bars.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"Stacked gold bullion bars\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Gold bars like these are exactly where Russia parked its trapped rupee earnings rather than reinvest them in India &#8212; the piece's central case study in who can, and cannot, spend the rupees they end up holding. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gold_bullion_bars.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Gold bullion bars.jpg</a>, Stevebidmead, CC0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "the-rupee-fell-10-and-exports-grew-09": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Mundra_port.jpg/960px-Mundra_port.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"Container terminal at Mundra Port, Gujarat\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Merchandise moving through ports like Mundra is the export volume this piece checks against a decade of rupee depreciation &#8212; and finds barely moved. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mundra_port.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mundra port.jpg</a>, Vijay8808, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "upi-fees-are-now-legal-petrol-pumps": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Indian_oil_Petrol_Pump_in_Marthandam.jpg/960px-Indian_oil_Petrol_Pump_in_Marthandam.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"An Indian Oil petrol pump forecourt\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Petrol pumps like this one are the merchant category this piece finds most exposed now that UPI's six-year fee shield has come off. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Indian_oil_Petrol_Pump_in_Marthandam.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Indian oil Petrol Pump in Marthandam.jpg</a>, Manukrishnan80, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "what-tepa-actually-opens-efta-goods": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Bullion_Gold_bar_at_Swiss_Money_Museum_%28Ank_Kumar%2C_Infosys%29.jpg/960px-Bullion_Gold_bar_at_Swiss_Money_Museum_%28Ank_Kumar%2C_Infosys%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"A gold bar displayed at the Swiss Money Museum\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Gold, not machinery or watches, is 89% of what India actually imports from Switzerland &#8212; and it's the one line TEPA's tariff schedule leaves untouched. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bullion_Gold_bar_at_Swiss_Money_Museum_(Ank_Kumar,_Infosys).jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Bullion Gold bar at Swiss Money Museum (Ank Kumar, Infosys).jpg</a>, Ank Kumar, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "rare-earth-magnets-and-specialty-steel": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Neodymium_magnet_-_19-11-2010.JPG/960px-Neodymium_magnet_-_19-11-2010.JPG?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"A neodymium rare-earth permanent magnet\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Sintered rare-earth magnets like this one are the exact component India's &#8377;7,200 crore scheme is trying to build a domestic supply chain for. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Neodymium_magnet_-_19-11-2010.JPG\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Neodymium magnet - 19-11-2010.JPG</a>, Tremaster at en.wikipedia, Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "indias-oil-fields-are-running-down-3696": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/ONGC_Oil_Platform.jpg/960px-ONGC_Oil_Platform.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"An ONGC offshore oil platform\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Platforms like this one, on ONGC's nomination acreage, are the fields DGH's own ten-year table shows falling from 36.96 to 28.70 MMT. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ONGC_Oil_Platform.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ONGC Oil Platform.jpg</a>, Nandu Chitnis from Pune, India, CC BY 2.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "india-cannot-sell-china-free-medicine": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Divis_Vizag_Jetty_entrance.jpg/960px-Divis_Vizag_Jetty_entrance.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"Entrance to a Divi's Laboratories facility in Visakhapatnam\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Divi's Laboratories is one of the bulk-drug makers the &#8377;6,940 crore PLI scheme was meant to wean off Chinese active ingredients, with limited results so far. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Divis_Vizag_Jetty_entrance.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Divis Vizag Jetty entrance.jpg</a>, Saiphani02, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "imported-fertiliser-fuel-prices-diesel": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Bharat_Petroleum_Petrol_Pump_near_Nagpur.jpg/960px-Bharat_Petroleum_Petrol_Pump_near_Nagpur.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"A Bharat Petroleum fuel station near Nagpur\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Diesel dispensed at pumps like this one is the WPI series this piece finds moving almost 1:1 with the wholesale price index, unlike subsidy-insulated urea. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bharat_Petroleum_Petrol_Pump_near_Nagpur.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Bharat Petroleum Petrol Pump near Nagpur.jpg</a>, Ganesh Dhamodkar, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "the-case-for-biofuels-over-imports": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fe/Shriram_sahkari_sakhar_karkhana.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\" alt=\"A cooperative sugar factory in Maharashtra\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Cooperative sugar mills like this one anchor the ethanol supply chain this piece argues should become the default fuel mix, not a blending mandate bolted onto petrol. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shriram_sahkari_sakhar_karkhana.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Shriram sahkari sakhar karkhana.jpg</a>, tadnya456, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "where-indias-factories-actually-get": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Jindal_steel_and_power_In_Kendujhar_district.png/960px-Jindal_steel_and_power_In_Kendujhar_district.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"A Jindal Steel and Power plant in Odisha's Kendujhar district\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Steel capex like Jindal's in Kendujhar is the domestic-capital story behind Odisha's #2 ranking in implemented industrial investment, built on just 0.14% of India's FDI. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jindal_steel_and_power_In_Kendujhar_district.png\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Jindal steel and power In Kendujhar district.png</a>, Bikashkumargiri1997, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "push-ethanol-sgst-rate-from-25-to-5-and": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/HP_Petrol_Pump_at_Addakal.jpg/960px-HP_Petrol_Pump_at_Addakal.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"An HP petrol pump forecourt in India\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Every litre sold at pumps like this one already carries 20% ethanol under the E20 mandate &#8212; the blend this piece's state-by-state SGST modelling is built on. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HP_Petrol_Pump_at_Addakal.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">HP Petrol Pump at Addakal.jpg</a>, Chanduclicks, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  }
}